@segment 22-24 Wetlands I
@start-level 22
# Human Warlock. From the Gnome route's segment 07 (class-neutral Alliance path): same quests, order, binds and
# flights. Changed: every combat hint is written for a warlock of level 22-24 (Voidwalker first, Corruption,
# Curse of Agony, Immolate, Fear on a second enemy, Drain Life, Health Funnel, Unending Breath for the dive);
# the optional training flight to Ironforge names Briarthorn in the Forlorn Cavern and has coordinates, the
# per-class ward list is gone. Segment numbers in the texts are this route's (the Gnome's plus one).
# Carry-in: 57, 67, 157, 181, 240, 453 (Duskwood and Westfall, segment 11), 455 (Algaz Gauntlet, handed in here).
# Carry-out: 57, 67, 157, 181, 240, 453 (segment 11), 275, 295, 471 (Wetlands, level 26-27, segment 10).
# Hearth: Thelsamar at the start, Menethil Harbor from the harbor on.
# Left out on purpose: 98459 A Lack of Virtue (ForeverChanges puts its giver, Tom "Half-fish" Wilson, in the
# Hillsbrad Foothills at 51.2, 66.5, not in the Wetlands), 463 The Greenwarden (you meet Rethiel before its giver),
# 1132 Fiora Longears (Theramore), 98190 A Friend of the Family (taken in segment 10), 161/274 (Dun Modr).
@carry 57,67,157,161,181,240,453,455,97894
@done 468

# ---------- Thelsamar -> Dun Algaz ----------
C 455 | From Thelsamar run the road north, past the northern guard tower and Mountaineer Rockgar, into the Dun Algaz tunnels. Finish what is still missing of 8 Dragonmaw Scouts (19-20) and 6 Dragonmaw Grunts (20-21) along the road and in the camps beside it, and walk the road all the way through to the Wetlands side.

# ---------- The Green Belt: Rethiel ----------
A 276 | Stay on the road where it leaves the hills and follow it north to the Green Belt. Rethiel the Greenwarden stands in the trees east of the road (56.4, 40.4).
C 276 @ Wetlands, 61.0, 68.0 | His gnolls live where you came out of the hills: Mosshide Gnolls (20-21) and Mosshide Mongrels (21-22) fill the marsh in the south-east, from the Dun Algaz road east to the waterfalls under the southern cliffs (54-67, 56-76). Go back south and kill 15 Gnolls and 10 Mongrels. They stand in small groups: send the Voidwalker at one from as far away as you can, let it hold the gnoll away from the others, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and wand. If a second one comes, the Voidwalker holds both, or Fear it, but only where it cannot run into another group: a feared gnoll brings friends. Gnolls run at low health and a warlock cannot slow them: keep your curses on and finish a runner with Shadow Bolt. Drain Life and Health Funnel keep you both up. Back off if a third one joins.
T 276 | Rethiel the Greenwarden
A 277 | Rethiel the Greenwarden
A 469 | Einar Stonegrip, the crocolisk hunter camped a little west of Rethiel, by the road (49.9, 39.4)
C 277 @ Wetlands, 51.0, 40.0 | 9 Crude Flints. Mosshide Fenrunners (22-23) carry them: they roam all around the Green Belt, on both sides of the road here. Mistweavers (22-23) drop them too: they are casters and a warlock has no interrupt, so kill them first, or Fear one while you finish another enemy. Black Oozes crawl around in the same marsh; they matter later, not now.
T 277 | Rethiel the Greenwarden
A 275 | Rethiel the Greenwarden. Fen Creepers are level 24-25 and hide in the waterways further north and west: kill the ones you happen to meet, and keep the quest for segment 10.

# ---------- Whelgar's Excavation Site and the raptors ----------
A 294 | Follow the road west, then leave it to the south for Whelgar's Excavation Site. Ormer Ironbraid stands at its entrance (38.2, 50.9). Needs level 22. Do not go down into the dig: the raptors there are 25-27.
C 294 @ Wetlands, 25.5, 49.5 | The raptors he wants live west of the dig, on both sides of the road to Menethil Harbor: kill 10 Mottled Raptors (22-23) and 10 Mottled Screechers (24-25). Screechers call for help, so let the Voidwalker hold them away from other raptors and kill them fast: Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, then Shadow Bolt. You hand this in when the big loop brings you back to Ormer.

# ---------- Menethil Harbor ----------
F Menethil Harbor @ Wetlands, 9.5, 59.7 | Keep west on the road to its end and cross the bridge into Menethil Harbor. Shellei Brondir, the gryphon master, stands by the docks.
S Menethil Harbor @ Wetlands, 10.7, 61.0 | Innkeeper Helbrek in the Deepwater Tavern
T 455 | Valstag Ironjaw, outside the keep in the middle of town
A 98197 | Valstag Ironjaw: Spoils of War (new in Forever)
C 98197 @ Wetlands, 10.1, 56.9 | Recover 6 Khaz Modan Timber and 30 Khaz Modan Iron from Menethil Harbor. The quest says they lie under water in the harbor; the data has no exact spots. Cast Unending Breath on yourself, dive around the docks and piers and look for timber and iron you can click. Renew Unending Breath when it runs out.
T 98197 | Valstag Ironjaw
T 469 | James Halloran, the tanner on the north-west side of town
A 484 | James Halloran
A 279 | Karl Boran, by the docks
A 98282 @ Wetlands, 11.9, 58.8 | Caitlin Grassman: Alchemical Hazards (new in Forever)
A 470 | Sida, next to her
A 305 | Tarrel Rockweaver, on the north side of town (needs level 21)

# ---------- The big loop ----------
C 279 | Leave by the bridge and go north along the coast. The Bluegill camp is at the river mouth (15.5, 40.1): kill 12 Bluegill Murlocs (20-21). Gobbler (22) walks at the east end of the camp (18.1, 39.8): loot his head. Other Bluegill types do not count for the 12 but come along if you pull carelessly: send the Voidwalker at one at a time and fight at the edge of the camp. Do not Fear inside the camp: a feared murloc brings the rest. Murlocs run at low health: keep Corruption and Curse of Agony on them and finish a runner with Shadow Bolt.
C 484 @ Wetlands, 30.0, 40.0 | Follow the river east. Young Wetlands Crocolisks (21-22) lie on its banks and in every waterway of the marsh: 4 skins. Leave the Wetlands Crocolisks (23-24) and Giant ones alone unless they come for you.
C 470 @ Wetlands, 44.4, 24.8 | Sida's Bag is inside an ooze. Kill every Black Ooze (23-24) you pass while you cross the marsh: they can carry it. If you still have no bag, go to Ironbeard's Tomb in the north (44.4, 24.8), where the Crimson Oozes (24-25) sit close together, and kill oozes there until it drops. Oozes hit slowly and are easy fights one at a time for the Voidwalker; use Drain Soul for the last hit on a few of them if you are short of Soul Shards (keep 3-5).
C 98282 | Cross to the south-east. Thelgen Rock is the spider cave in the cliffs south of the Green Belt (around 50, 62). Kill Leech Stalkers and Cave Stalkers (21-22) inside and in front of the cave until one drops an Unruptured Stalker Gland. They poison you and a warlock cannot cure poison: let the Voidwalker take the bites, use Drain Life in the fight, and bandage and eat between fights. Leave the Leech Widow (24 elite) deeper inside alone.
T 305 | Back north-west to Whelgar's Excavation Site. Merrin Rockweaver stands near Ormer at the entrance (38.9, 52.3).
A 306 | Merrin Rockweaver
T 294 | Ormer Ironbraid
A 295 | Ormer Ironbraid. Scytheclaws and Razormaws are 25-27: kept for segment 10.

# ---------- Menethil Harbor hand-ins ----------
T 306 | Take the road back to Menethil Harbor. Tarrel Rockweaver, on the north side of town.
T 484 | James Halloran
A 471 | James Halloran. Giant Crocolisks are 25-26: kept for segment 10.
T 279 | Karl Boran
A 281 | Karl Boran
T 98282 @ Wetlands, 11.9, 58.8 | Caitlin Grassman
T 470 | Sida

# ---------- The murloc camps and the statuette ----------
T 281 | Back to the Bluegill camps on the coast north of town. Click the Damaged Crate (13.5, 41.4).
A 284 | From the Damaged Crate
T 284 | The Sealed Barrel, a little further north (13.6, 38.2)
A 285 | From the Sealed Barrel
T 285 | The Half-buried Barrel in the northern camp (13.9, 34.8). Murlocs stand right next to each container: clear them first with the Voidwalker, a click is interrupted when you are hit.
A 286 | From the Half-buried Barrel
T 286 | Karl Boran, by the Menethil docks
A 98189 | Karl Boran: Return the Statuette (new in Forever)
T 98189 | Captain Stoutfist, inside Menethil Keep. Do not take his other quests yet: they belong to segment 10.

# ---------- Training (optional) and the boat ----------
TRAIN @ Ironforge, 50.4, 5.7 | Optional, about 10 minutes: fly from Menethil Harbor to Ironforge and back. Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn everything he offers at level 24, and look at the demon trainer beside him for new Voidwalker spell books. The route's next training stop is Ironforge at level 28. Press Skip if you would rather go on.
N Take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine | Buy food and water first. Not verified for Forever: a quest text says the Auberdine boat stops in Southshore on the way over. If it does, stay on board until Auberdine in Darkshore.
